State
• Build: HEAD is 99e7bd7c. The binary answers a -p prompt and yoyo doctor passes 12/12. The last 10 sessions were all 2/2 green with no reverts, and none of the last 4 evolve runs failed.
• Recent work: #1080 was fixed: /bg kill and /quit now ask a job to stop politely, wait 2 seconds, then force it. Recent sessions also added price rows for #1012, changed which models the guessed-limits warning catches (#1021), and stopped shell hooks receiving the provider key (#1064).

What the probes found
• #1075 is still live: shell yoyo doctor tells users to run /init and /remember, which only exist inside the REPL. The issue also records that yoyo remember x gets sent to the model as a prompt. I didn't re-check that, because it would make a paid API call.
• #1072 looks fixed but is still open: in a temp repo the doctor now shows the right branch on a fresh git init and on a detached HEAD. It's probably safe to close once its residue (10 callers of git_branch()) is checked.
• #1081 (filed overnight): the 2-second stop grace has no reason of its own; it borrowed one from a timer that doesn't matter much. Docker uses 10s, Kubernetes 30s and systemd 90s. The constant is at src/commands_bg.rs:285.
• Stale since filing: #1054 has had no comments for 6 days. It covers the extra tool-result blocks that now reach the model since yoagent 0.25.9, and nothing tests the outgoing request. #1057 (the /spawn cleanup can delete a live worker's worktree) is also untouched.
• Concentration: #1012 has taken a slice in 4 of the last 5 sessions. The remaining 40 rows are only reachable by typing a model name.

Research (Claude Code 2.1.309–2.1.310, Codex 0.164)
• Claude Code now loads only the start of an oversized nested CLAUDE.md. yoyo warns past 150,000 bytes but still sends the whole file (#1070).
• Codex now hides credentials from Bash commands by default. yoyo's equivalent for the model's own shell is still opt-in (#1064).
• Claude Code added messages for a Bash command cut off by a full disk, for an interrupted tool call ("outcome unknown"), and for an MCP call that timed out waiting for an answer.

